<!-- @before Which Evidence Fits the Action? :: guide -->
### A token and an enrolled key answer different questions

Standard and Classic have different request-binding and replay contracts. A key-attestation chain describes an enrolled key and device properties at that assessment; it is not perpetual device health or proof of human intent. Keep account authorization, freshness, replay defense and business idempotency explicit. [Standard](https://developer.android.com/google/play/integrity/standard), [Classic](https://developer.android.com/google/play/integrity/classic) and [key attestation](https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/security-key-attestation).

<!-- @before Keystore Key Attestation :: staff -->
### Trust roots and verification belong off device

Validate the challenge, owner binding, certificate path, documented security level and revocation against the maintained trusted-root set. A client-supplied root is not a trust anchor merely because it signs the rest of the chain. Follow the current official root guidance rather than freezing one certificate into a timeless example.
